WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.400
METE ATAMEL: Let's
deploy an ASP.NET Core

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.100
app to a Kubernetes cluster
on Google Container Engine.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.125
First, in Cloud Shell,
create a Kubernetes cluster.

00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:16.660
As cluster is setting up,
create an ASP.NET Core web app.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.740
Restore and publish the app
to get a self-contained DLO.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.970
Inside publish folder,
create a Dockerfile.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:25.960
Dockerfile builds on
the official Google

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.080
image for ASP.NET Core apps.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.619
Build local image using
Google Container Builder.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:34.870
This publishes the image
to Google Container

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:39.530
repository that we can use from
our Kubernetes cluster later.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:48.490
Finally, create a Kubernetes
deployment with the image

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:50.350
and expose it to
the outside world.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:58.460
In a few seconds, your app
will be running in Kubernetes.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:00.310
Thanks for watching.

